:Namespace state
    ⍝ State Machine Enumeration based off of "My Favorite Verbose Programming Technique"
    ⍝ https://github.com/Co-dfns/APL-Asteroids
    ⍝ Was previously doing namespace swapping for state handling
    ⍝ -- Want to see if there is any perceivable benefit of doing this instead.


    ⍝ Overall pattern:
    ⍝ - Each state has a mini-event loop that is exhausted before
    ⍝   being updated and drawn, hence %_EVENT_ precedes %_.
    ⍝   This is an equivalent of "while polling check if input" but
    ⍝   'unrolled.'
    ⍝
    ⍝ - A helper operator that checks if user is quitting or if window is
    ⍝   resized is added to make this process a bit easier.
    ⍝
    ⍝ - Menu and Saves share the same resources but are different
    ⍝   enough in logic to be conceptually split up, hence they go to
    ⍝   the same release function.


    (TICK QUIT BACK NEXT) ← 1+⍳4

    ∇ Game_loop core
     
      ##.menu_state.Init core
     
     ⍝ ----------
     ⍝ Menu State
     ⍝ ----------
     
     ∆_MENU_EVENT_:→⎕LC+##.menu_state.Input _Exhaust_with core
     ∆_MENU_EVENT_TICK:→∆_MENU_EVENT_
     ∆_MENU_EVENT_QUIT:→∆_MENU_QUIT
     ∆_MENU_EVENT_BACK:∘∘∘
     ∆_MENU_EVENT_NEXT:→∆_MENU_
     
     ∆_MENU_:→⎕LC+##.menu_state.Loop_menu core
     ∆_MENU_TICK:→∆_MENU_EVENT_
     ∆_MENU_QUIT:##.menu_state.Release core ⋄ →0
     ∆_MENU_BACK:∘∘∘
     ∆_MENU_NEXT:→∆_SAVES_EVENT_
     
     ⍝ -----------
     ⍝ Saves State
     ⍝ -----------
     
     ∆_SAVES_EVENT_:→⎕LC+##.menu_state.Input _Exhaust_with core
     ∆_SAVES_EVENT_TICK:→∆_SAVES_EVENT_
     ∆_SAVES_EVENT_QUIT:→∆_MENU_QUIT
     ∆_SAVES_EVENT_BACK:∘∘∘
     ∆_SAVES_EVENT_NEXT:→∆_SAVES_
     
     ∆_SAVES_:→⎕LC+##.menu_state.Loop_saves core
     ∆_SAVES_TICK:→∆_SAVES_EVENT_
     ∆_SAVES_QUIT:→∆_MENU_QUIT
     ∆_SAVES_BACK:→∆_MENU_
     ∆_SAVES_NEXT:Saves_to_world core ⋄ →∆_WORLD_EVENT_
     
     ⍝ -----------
     ⍝ World State
     ⍝ -----------
     
     ∆_WORLD_EVENT_:→⎕LC+##.world_state.Input _Exhaust_with core
     ∆_WORLD_EVENT_TICK:→∆_WORLD_EVENT_
     ∆_WORLD_EVENT_QUIT:→∆_WORLD_QUIT
     ∆_WORLD_EVENT_BACK:∘∘∘
     ∆_WORLD_EVENT_NEXT:→∆_WORLD_
     
     ∆_WORLD_:→⎕LC+##.world_state.Loop core
     ∆_WORLD_TICK:→∆_WORLD_EVENT_
     ∆_WORLD_QUIT:##.world_state.Release core ⋄ →0
     ∆_WORLD_BACK:∘∘∘
     ∆_WORLD_NEXT:∘∘∘
    ∇

    ∇ Saves_to_world core;save
      save←##.menu_state.next_world
      ##.menu_state.Release core
      ##.world_state.Init core save
    ∇

    ∇ a←(Exhaust_fn _Exhaust_with)core
      a←TICK
      :If 0=⊃##.LSE_PollEvent
          a←NEXT
          :Return
      :EndIf
      :If ##.LSE_CheckEvent ##.SDL_EVENT_QUIT
          a←QUIT
      :ElseIf ##.LSE_CheckEvent ##.SDL_EVENT_KEY_DOWN
          :If ##.SDLK_Q=⊃##.LSE_GetKeyPressed ⍬
              a←QUIT
          :EndIf
      :ElseIf ##.LSE_CheckEvent ##.SDL_EVENT_WINDOW_RESIZED
          (core.w core.h)←##.LSE_GetWindowResize 0 0
      :EndIf
     
      Exhaust_fn core
    ∇

    ∇ Play
      res←##.SDL_Init ##.SDL_INIT_VIDEO
      'Error initializing SDL3'##.Assert res
     
      window←##.SDL_CreateWindow'A Voxel Game' 1280 720 32
      'Error creating window'##.Assert window
     
      device←##.SDL_CreateGPUDevice(
          ##.Get_shader_format ⍬
          1
          ##.Get_device_backend ⍬
      )
      'Error creating GPU device'##.Assert device
      res←##.SDL_ClaimWindowForGPUDevice device window
      'Error attaching GPU device to window'##.Assert res
      ##.block_data.Init device
      ##.text.Init device window
      core_data←(
          window:window
          device:device
          w:1280
          h:720
          dt:÷60
          save:''
      )
     
      Game_loop core_data
     
      ##.text.Release device
      ##.block_data.Release device
      _←##.SDL_ReleaseWindowFromGPUDevice device window
      _←##.SDL_DestroyGPUDevice device
      _←##.SDL_DestroyWindow window
      ⍝ https://github.com/libsdl-org/SDL/issues/10081#issuecomment-2570813902
      _←##.SDL_PumpEvents
      _←##.SDL_Quit
    ∇

:EndNamespace
